[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":2115},["ShallowReactive",2],{"article-setting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3":3,"articles-100":1937,"topic-of-article-setting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3":2077,"articles-10":2094},{"id":4,"title":5,"alt":6,"body":7,"description":1921,"extension":1922,"image":1923,"meta":1924,"navigation":162,"path":1925,"postDate":1926,"published":1927,"seo":1928,"stem":1929,"tags":1930,"topic":1934,"updated":1935,"url":1935,"__hash__":1936},"blog\u002Fblog\u002Fsetting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3.md","Why I added RSS feeds to my blog (and how I did it in Nuxt 3)","RSS and Atom feeds in Nuxt 3",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":1905},"minimark",[10,15,25,35,39,42,45,48,52,55,58,62,70,113,117,122,129,365,375,379,385,1375,1379,1382,1388,1519,1524,1639,1649,1653,1659,1777,1781,1784,1788,1794,1852,1856,1859,1886,1890,1893,1901],[11,12,14],"h2",{"id":13},"what-are-rss-and-atom-feeds","What are RSS and Atom feeds?",[16,17,18,19,24],"p",{},"RSS (Really Simple Syndication) and Atom are XML formats for sharing new posts with readers. Instead of visiting each site by hand, readers subscribe to a feed. When a site publishes new content, the feed updates and readers see it in their feed reader. I use ",[20,21,23],"a",{"href":22},"\u002Fblog\u002Freading-and-discovery-feed-curation\u002F","a self-hosted FreshRSS"," for mine.",[16,26,27,28,34],{},"Some popular web-based feed readers are FreshRSS, Feedly, Inoreader, and NewsBlur. Desktop apps like Fluent Reader and mobile apps like Reeder and Readrops are also available. I run a ",[20,29,33],{"href":30,"rel":31},"https:\u002F\u002Ffreshrss.org\u002F",[32],"nofollow","FreshRSS"," instance in my homelab and read updates through its web UI or the Readrops app on my phone.",[11,36,38],{"id":37},"the-rise-fall-and-resurgence-of-rssatom","The rise, fall, and resurgence of RSS\u002FAtom",[16,40,41],{},"In the early days, RSS was everywhere. Blogs and news sites all used it, and podcasts did too. Most people, including me, relied on feed readers to keep up with their favorite sites. Feeds were a simple and effective way to follow online content.",[16,43,44],{},"Then social platforms came along. They promised to show us content based on our interests using recommendation algorithms. When Google Reader (a prominent feed reader at the time) shut down in 2013, it marked a shift in how we read online. Like many others, I switched to getting my news and updates from social media.",[16,46,47],{},"After seeing how social media algorithms favor engagement over user interests, some of us started going back to RSS. While it's not perfect, I prefer the straightforward approach of choosing what I want to read rather than having it chosen for me.",[11,49,51],{"id":50},"adding-feeds-to-my-blog","Adding feeds to my blog",[16,53,54],{},"Since I started using RSS feeds again, I wanted my Nuxt 3 blog to support both feed formats. I went with both formats because some feed readers are picky. Since the library generates the feeds, the extra few lines of code don't add much.",[16,56,57],{},"Here's how I added RSS and Atom feeds to my blog:",[11,59,61],{"id":60},"setting-up-the-feed-package","Setting up the feed package",[16,63,64,65,69],{},"The first step was installing the ",[66,67,68],"code",{},"feed"," package:",[71,72,77],"pre",{"className":73,"code":74,"language":75,"meta":76,"style":76},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","npm install feed\n# or with yarn\nyarn add feed\n","bash","",[66,78,79,95,102],{"__ignoreMap":76},[80,81,84,88,92],"span",{"class":82,"line":83},"line",1,[80,85,87],{"class":86},"sScJk","npm",[80,89,91],{"class":90},"sZZnC"," install",[80,93,94],{"class":90}," feed\n",[80,96,98],{"class":82,"line":97},2,[80,99,101],{"class":100},"sJ8bj","# or with yarn\n",[80,103,105,108,111],{"class":82,"line":104},3,[80,106,107],{"class":86},"yarn",[80,109,110],{"class":90}," add",[80,112,94],{"class":90},[11,114,116],{"id":115},"creating-the-feed-system","Creating the feed system",[118,119,121],"h3",{"id":120},"fetching-blog-posts","Fetching blog posts",[16,123,124,125,128],{},"I started by creating a function to fetch my blog posts. Here's what I put in ",[66,126,127],{},"server\u002Futils\u002Fblog.ts",":",[71,130,134],{"className":131,"code":132,"language":133,"meta":76,"style":76},"language-typescript shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","import type { BlogPostPreview } from \"~\u002Ftypes\";\n\nexport async function getBlogPosts(event: any): Promise\u003CBlogPostPreview[]> {\n  try {\n    \u002F\u002F event parameter is required for server-side content querying\n    return await queryCollection(event, \"blog\")\n      .select(\"title\", \"description\", \"tags\", \"postDate\", \"path\", \"url\")\n      .order(\"postDate\", \"DESC\")\n      .all();\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching blog posts:\", e);\n    return [];\n  }\n}\n","typescript",[66,135,136,158,164,208,217,223,244,286,305,316,328,345,353,359],{"__ignoreMap":76},[80,137,138,142,145,149,152,155],{"class":82,"line":83},[80,139,141],{"class":140},"szBVR","import",[80,143,144],{"class":140}," type",[80,146,148],{"class":147},"sVt8B"," { BlogPostPreview } ",[80,150,151],{"class":140},"from",[80,153,154],{"class":90}," \"~\u002Ftypes\"",[80,156,157],{"class":147},";\n",[80,159,160],{"class":82,"line":97},[80,161,163],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":162},true,"\n",[80,165,166,169,172,175,178,181,185,187,191,194,196,199,202,205],{"class":82,"line":104},[80,167,168],{"class":140},"export",[80,170,171],{"class":140}," async",[80,173,174],{"class":140}," function",[80,176,177],{"class":86}," getBlogPosts",[80,179,180],{"class":147},"(",[80,182,184],{"class":183},"s4XuR","event",[80,186,128],{"class":140},[80,188,190],{"class":189},"sj4cs"," any",[80,192,193],{"class":147},")",[80,195,128],{"class":140},[80,197,198],{"class":86}," Promise",[80,200,201],{"class":147},"\u003C",[80,203,204],{"class":86},"BlogPostPreview",[80,206,207],{"class":147},"[]> {\n",[80,209,211,214],{"class":82,"line":210},4,[80,212,213],{"class":140},"  try",[80,215,216],{"class":147}," {\n",[80,218,220],{"class":82,"line":219},5,[80,221,222],{"class":100},"    \u002F\u002F event parameter is required for server-side content querying\n",[80,224,226,229,232,235,238,241],{"class":82,"line":225},6,[80,227,228],{"class":140},"    return",[80,230,231],{"class":140}," await",[80,233,234],{"class":86}," queryCollection",[80,236,237],{"class":147},"(event, ",[80,239,240],{"class":90},"\"blog\"",[80,242,243],{"class":147},")\n",[80,245,247,250,253,255,258,261,264,266,269,271,274,276,279,281,284],{"class":82,"line":246},7,[80,248,249],{"class":147},"      .",[80,251,252],{"class":86},"select",[80,254,180],{"class":147},[80,256,257],{"class":90},"\"title\"",[80,259,260],{"class":147},", ",[80,262,263],{"class":90},"\"description\"",[80,265,260],{"class":147},[80,267,268],{"class":90},"\"tags\"",[80,270,260],{"class":147},[80,272,273],{"class":90},"\"postDate\"",[80,275,260],{"class":147},[80,277,278],{"class":90},"\"path\"",[80,280,260],{"class":147},[80,282,283],{"class":90},"\"url\"",[80,285,243],{"class":147},[80,287,289,291,294,296,298,300,303],{"class":82,"line":288},8,[80,290,249],{"class":147},[80,292,293],{"class":86},"order",[80,295,180],{"class":147},[80,297,273],{"class":90},[80,299,260],{"class":147},[80,301,302],{"class":90},"\"DESC\"",[80,304,243],{"class":147},[80,306,308,310,313],{"class":82,"line":307},9,[80,309,249],{"class":147},[80,311,312],{"class":86},"all",[80,314,315],{"class":147},"();\n",[80,317,319,322,325],{"class":82,"line":318},10,[80,320,321],{"class":147},"  } ",[80,323,324],{"class":140},"catch",[80,326,327],{"class":147}," (e) {\n",[80,329,331,334,337,339,342],{"class":82,"line":330},11,[80,332,333],{"class":147},"    console.",[80,335,336],{"class":86},"error",[80,338,180],{"class":147},[80,340,341],{"class":90},"\"Error fetching blog posts:\"",[80,343,344],{"class":147},", e);\n",[80,346,348,350],{"class":82,"line":347},12,[80,349,228],{"class":140},[80,351,352],{"class":147}," [];\n",[80,354,356],{"class":82,"line":355},13,[80,357,358],{"class":147},"  }\n",[80,360,362],{"class":82,"line":361},14,[80,363,364],{"class":147},"}\n",[16,366,367,368,370,371,374],{},"It took me a while to figure this out: on the server-side, we also need to pass the ",[66,369,184],{}," parameter to ",[66,372,373],{},"queryCollection"," to access the server request context. Client-side code doesn't need this.",[118,376,378],{"id":377},"generating-the-feeds","Generating the feeds",[16,380,381,382,128],{},"Next, I needed functions to generate the actual feeds. Here's what I created in ",[66,383,384],{},"server\u002Futils\u002Ffeed.ts",[71,386,388],{"className":131,"code":387,"language":133,"meta":76,"style":76},"\u002F\u002F Import Feed library and our blog post type\nimport { Feed } from \"feed\";\nimport type { BlogPostPreview } from \"~\u002Ftypes\";\n\nexport type FeedFormat = \"rss\" | \"atom\";\n\n\u002F\u002F Default feed metadata - customize these values\nconst DEFAULT_TITLE = \"Your Site Name\";\nconst DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION = \"Your site description\";\n\n\u002F\u002F Creates a new Feed instance with common configuration\nexport function createBaseFeed(baseUrl: string) {\n  if (!baseUrl) {\n    throw new Error(\"Base URL is required to create a feed\");\n  }\n\n  return new Feed({\n    title: DEFAULT_TITLE,\n    id: baseUrl,\n    link: baseUrl,\n    description: DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION,\n    language: \"en\",\n    copyright: `Copyright ${new Date().getFullYear()} Your Name`,\n    \u002F\u002F Advertise both feed formats\n    feedLinks: {\n      rss2: `${baseUrl}\u002Frss.xml`,\n      atom: `${baseUrl}\u002Fatom.xml`,\n    },\n    author: {\n      name: DEFAULT_TITLE,\n      link: baseUrl,\n    },\n    updated: new Date(), \u002F\u002F Required for Atom feeds\n  });\n}\n\n\u002F\u002F Adds blog posts to the feed with proper metadata\nexport function addPostsToFeed(\n  feed: Feed,\n  posts: BlogPostPreview[],\n  baseUrl: string,\n) {\n  if (!feed || !Array.isArray(posts) || !baseUrl) {\n    throw new Error(\"Feed, posts array, and base URL are required\");\n  }\n\n  for (const post of posts) {\n    \u002F\u002F Skip posts without required fields\n    if (!post.title || !post.path) {\n      console.warn(\"Skipping invalid post:\", post);\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    \u002F\u002F Add post to feed with full metadata\n    feed.addItem({\n      title: post.title,\n      id: `${baseUrl}${post.path}`, \u002F\u002F Unique identifier\n      link: `${baseUrl}${post.path}`, \u002F\u002F Full URL to post\n      description: post.description || \"\",\n      date: new Date(post.postDate || Date.now()),\n      category: post.tags?.map((tag) => ({ name: tag })) || [],\n      author: [\n        {\n          name: DEFAULT_TITLE,\n          link: baseUrl,\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n\u002F\u002F Unified feed generation function\nexport async function generateFeed(\n  event: any,\n  baseUrl: string,\n  format: FeedFormat,\n): Promise\u003Cstring> {\n  try {\n    const blogPosts = await getBlogPosts(event);\n    const feed = createBaseFeed(baseUrl);\n    addPostsToFeed(feed, blogPosts, baseUrl);\n\n    return format === \"rss\" ? feed.rss2() : feed.atom1();\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`Error generating ${format} feed:`, error);\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n",[66,389,390,395,409,423,427,450,454,459,474,488,492,497,519,533,552,557,562,576,588,594,600,611,622,651,657,663,679,694,700,706,716,722,727,743,749,754,759,765,778,790,804,816,821,854,870,875,880,899,905,925,942,950,956,961,967,978,984,1014,1039,1052,1076,1105,1111,1117,1127,1133,1139,1145,1151,1156,1161,1166,1172,1186,1198,1209,1221,1238,1245,1263,1278,1287,1292,1326,1336,1357,1365,1370],{"__ignoreMap":76},[80,391,392],{"class":82,"line":83},[80,393,394],{"class":100},"\u002F\u002F Import Feed library and our blog post type\n",[80,396,397,399,402,404,407],{"class":82,"line":97},[80,398,141],{"class":140},[80,400,401],{"class":147}," { Fee