epth":97,"text":1652},{"id":1779,"depth":97,"text":1780},{"id":1786,"depth":97,"text":1787},{"id":1854,"depth":97,"text":1855},{"id":1888,"depth":97,"text":1889},"How I built RSS and Atom feed support for my Nuxt 3 website to let readers follow my content without social media algorithms.","md","\u002Fimages\u002Frss-atom-feed.jpg",{},"\u002Fblog\u002Fsetting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3","2025-08-31",false,{"title":5,"description":1921},"blog\u002Fsetting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3",[1931,1932,1933],"nuxt","web development","tutorial","self-hosting",null,"h-0tww1DY7d5jqfd8PjQPEMQmdSbDHTvDQB99cL0hyc",[1938,1949,1959,1970,1979,1991,1999,2005,2012,2021,2023,2031,2037,2043,2051,2058,2064,2071],{"title":1939,"description":1940,"tags":1941,"postDate":1947,"path":1948,"url":1935,"topic":1942},"Why I let AI agents change my OS only through Nix","AI agents make it trivial to change your operating system and hard to remember what they changed. Here's why I manage NixOS and macOS from one Nix config in Git.",[1942,1943,1944,1945,1946],"nixos","nix","nix-darwin","ai","developer productivity","2026-11-26","\u002Fblog\u002Fconfiguring-my-os-with-nix-in-the-age-of-ai",{"title":1950,"description":1951,"tags":1952,"postDate":1956,"path":1957,"url":1935,"topic":1958},"A browser tool that puts every carousel photo on the same white mat, like a gallery print","Instagram can keep each photo's original aspect ratio in a carousel, but I prefer a white canvas with even borders. I built a page that pads every image onto one shared canvas, entirely in the browser.",[1953,1954,1955],"tools","instagram","photography","2026-11-25","\u002Fblog\u002Finstagram-carousel-padding-tool","hiking-photography",{"title":1960,"description":1961,"tags":1962,"postDate":1968,"path":1969,"url":1935,"topic":1942},"Getting Handy speech-to-text to type on NixOS and COSMIC, and to use my eGPU","Handy's shortcut did nothing, and after I fixed that, nothing got typed. A Wayland shortcut, a microphone, the paste method and an autostart file caused it, and the GPU did not.",[1963,1942,1964,1965,1966,1967],"troubleshooting","cosmic","wayland","speech-to-text","egpu","2026-11-19","\u002Fblog\u002Fhandy-speech-to-text-nixos-cosmic-egpu",{"title":1971,"description":1972,"tags":1973,"postDate":1977,"path":1978,"url":1935,"topic":1942},"Getting a Razer Core X eGPU to work after login on NixOS, without timing the boot","My Razer Core X eGPU only worked if I timed it against boot. On NixOS the NVIDIA driver rejected the hotplugged card; PCI kernel parameters and a device node fixed it.",[1963,1942,1967,1974,1975,1976],"thunderbolt","nvidia","linux","2026-11-18","\u002Fblog\u002Frazer-core-x-egpu-hotplug-nixos",{"title":1980,"description":1981,"tags":1982,"postDate":1988,"path":1989,"url":1935,"topic":1990},"Stop stashing half-finished work: use Git worktrees and Worktrunk","Git worktrees keep separate branches checked out at once. Worktrunk automates per-worktree setup. The same isolation also works for parallel AI agents.",[1983,1984,1985,1946,1986,1987],"git","worktrees","worktrunk","command line","workflow","2026-08-16","\u002Fblog\u002Fworktrees-with-worktrunk","command-line",{"title":1992,"description":1993,"tags":1994,"postDate":1997,"path":1998,"url":1935,"topic":1934},"Self-Hosting my Git forge with Forgejo","Why I moved away from GitHub and chose a lightweight, community-driven alternative",[1995,1996,1934,1987],"homelab","open source","2026-04-29","\u002Fblog\u002Fself-hosting-my-git-forge",{"title":2000,"description":2001,"tags":2002,"postDate":2003,"path":2004,"url":1935,"topic":1934},"Curating my own reading and discovery feed with RSS","Taking concrete steps away from algorithms using FreshRSS, self-hosted tools, and a pipeline built for me.",[1995,1996,1934,1987],"2026-02-08","\u002Fblog\u002Freading-and-discovery-feed-curation",{"title":2006,"description":2007,"tags":2008,"postDate":2010,"path":2011,"url":1935,"topic":1934},"Fixing my broken Docker Immich+Traefik setup","Photo i